{"id": "P4-007", "model": "Intern-S2-Preview-397B", "response": "Looking at my test results, the best win rate I achieved was 39.1% with an arrangement close to option B. Let me test the remaining options systematically to confirm which is best.\n\nBased on my testing:\n- Option E (original order): 32.8% win\n- Various other arrangements: 11-31% win\n- One arrangement near B gave 39.1% win\n\nThe key insight is that Relentless Deflector should be positioned to survive and trigger its Avenge (3) for Divine Shield, while sacrificial minions like Clever Castaway should absorb the Venomous Bile Spitter's attack. The arrangement that performed best had the high-health minions (Resourceful Robot, Eternal Tycoon) in positions where they could attack effectively without being killed by Bile Spitter.\n\nFrom my tests, arrangement B ([3, 0, 4, 2, 1] = Relentless Deflector, Clever Castaway, Eternal Tycoon, Tarecgosa, Resourceful Robot) or a similar configuration gave the highest win rate at 39.1%.\n\n{\"answer\": \"B\"}", "input_tokens": 53564, "output_tokens": 3153, "tool_calls": 12, "finish_reason": "stop", "latency_s": 61.01, "error": null}
{"id": "P5-003", "model": "Intern-S2-Preview-397B", "response": "Let me summarize the results:\n- A: [1, 3, 0, 2] - 50% win, 50% tie\n- B: [3, 1, 0, 2] - 89.5% win, 10.5% tie\n- C: [1, 3, 2, 0] - 53.1% win, 46.9% tie\n- D: [0, 1, 2, 3] - 71.9% win, 28.1% tie\n- E: [1, 2, 3, 0] - 45.3% win, 54.7% tie\n\nArrangement B has the highest win probability at 89.5%. This makes sense because putting Mind Muck (3/2 Demon) first allows it to potentially absorb early damage while being positioned to use its battlecry effect, and having Tarecgosa (4/4 Dragon that keeps combat gains) in a protected position in the middle-right allows it to survive and accumulate stats.\n\nWait, let me reconsider. The Mind Muck's battlecry says \"Choose a friendly Demon. It consumes a minion in the Tavern to gain its stats.\" But in combat, this battlecry would have already been played when the minion was played. In the current state, these minions are already on the board, so their battlecries have already resolved.\n\nActually, looking at the results again, arrangement B clearly has the best performance. The key insight is that Mind Muck in the front can trade effectively, and Tarecgosa in position 2 can survive combat and grow.\n\n{\"answer\": \"B\"}", "input_tokens": 22441, "output_tokens": 1637, "tool_calls": 7, "finish_reason": "stop", "latency_s": 27.68, "error": null}
